/*****************************************************************************
    jitJRt3 -- F3. CLAIM KANT-8's SHAPE, JITTED. AN INTENDED DIVERGENCE, BORN
    AS A FIXTURE. 2026-08-05.

    ⚠⚠ THIS ROW IS EXPECTED TO DISAGREE WITH THE INTERPRETER, BY DESIGN. It is
    KR-3's first inverted row. Tony's ruling, item 2, 2026-08-05: the returned
    value arrives intact under the JIT, and there is NO PARITY OBLIGATION to the
    interpreter's KANT-8 behaviour -- an intended divergence is a LEDGER ROW,
    not a defect. Do not "fix" this fixture to agree.

    THE SHAPE IS incant/kant8T's K1: recursive, returns a LOCAL.
        interpreted   returns the bare TAG `k8loc` -- the local is EMPTIED by
                      saveLocalFields, and a field with no data returns its tag
                      from .text, so the local is genuinely blanked rather than
                      zeroed (kant8T, measured 2026-08-05)
        jitted        returns 42 -- a jitted scalar local is an ALLOCA in the
                      compiled function, so it is per-activation FOR FREE. The
                      JIT does not inherit the bug because it does not inherit
                      the mechanism.

    ⚠ AND K4 SHARPENS WHY THIS IS NOT A NARROW CASE: `recursive` is a STATIC
    flag set at parse time by identity, so the interpreter's bracket runs on
    EVERY call of an action that merely MENTIONS ITS OWN NAME -- recursion taken
    or not. The interpreted column here is the normal case, not a corner.

    ⚠ THE RETURNED LOCAL IS INPUT-DEPENDENT ON PURPOSE. k8loc = k8n + 40, so
    fire 1 (k8n=2) returns 42 and fire 2 (k8n=5) returns 45. A constant 42 on
    both fires would satisfy the brief's number and prove nothing about WHEN it
    was computed; two different answers are the injectivity rule.

    GATED, NOT BLOCKING: KANT-8's own repair and the frame-model ruling remain
    behind kant8T's K5/K6 extension. This fixture asserts the JIT's column only.

    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT, exactly ONE stop() (rule H2).
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;
register(JitLadder);
define
    k8n;
    k8 code={
        k8loc = k8n + 40;
        if k8n > 0;
            k8n = k8n - 1;
            k8();
        return k8loc;
        };
    ;
k8n = 2;
print "JRt3 fire 1 setup : k8n =" k8n:;
testing(k8);

k8n = 5;
print "JRt3 fire 2 setup : k8n =" k8n " (recompile: NONE)":;
jitRefire();

print "JRt3 SENTINEL":;
stop();
